    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Why records were rejected",
      "description": "A FULL OUTER JOIN, so a reason only one engine produces still appears, with a zero on the other side -- the case an inner join would hide, and the most serious one, because it means an engine is missing a rule. Sorted by the size of the difference, so anything non-zero is the first row.",
